\[
\frac{\tan x}{\sec x+1}-\frac{\sec x-1}{\tan x}
= \frac{\tan x(\sec x-1)}{(\sec x+1)(\sec x-1)}-\frac{\sec x-1}{\tan x}
\]

Since \((\sec x+1)(\sec x-1)=\sec^2 x-1=\tan^2 x\),

\[
\frac{\tan x(\sec x-1)}{\tan^2 x}=\frac{\sec x-1}{\tan x}
\]

Thus the expression simplifies to

\[
\boxed{0}
\]
